  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient adaptation through distributed and cold storage in the Republic of the Gambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project provides an urgent response to climate-induced food insecurity in the Gambia, where repeated floods and droughts have d evastated harvests and destroyed critical storage infrastructure in vulnerable rural areas. By replacing damaged storage facilities and deploying decentralised cold storage systems, the initiative aims to immediately reduce post-harvest losses while stabilising local food security. The project uniquely integrates innovative solutions from Japanese small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), showcasing their potential to address complex development challenges through tailored, field-tested technologies. It also lays the foundation for long-term climate resilience  and contributes to Japan#s broader development cooperation objectives, including human security, food system strengthening, and local co-creation under TICAD  frameworks.</narrative>
  </description>
